      ":question/problem": "![](images/c4/c4b26c7ea6f872ba0a21b2950ace0aa467fd630c52c302bd0017bcedaadee5b2.png)\n\nIn the diagram, $Z$ lies on the segment $GN$. The given vectors are $\\overrightarrow{OG}=h$ and $\\overrightarrow{ON}=d$. The lengths satisfy $GZ:ZN=5:7$.\n\nExpress $\\overrightarrow{OZ}$ in terms of $h$ and $d$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First express both endpoint vectors in the directions away from $O$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OG}=h\\qquad \\overrightarrow{ON}=d .\n$$\n\nTrace the path from $G$ through $O$ to $N$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{GN}=\\overrightarrow{GO}+\\overrightarrow{ON}=-h+d.\n$$\n\nThe ratio $GZ:ZN=5:7$ gives $12$ parts in the whole segment. Thus\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{GZ}=\\frac{5}{12}\\overrightarrow{GN}=\\frac{5}{12}(-h+d).\n$$\n\nAdd along the path $O\\to G\\to Z$ and collect coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overrightarrow{OZ}&=\\overrightarrow{OG}+\\overrightarrow{GZ}\\\\&=h+\\frac{5}{12}(-h+d)\\\\&=\\frac{7}{12}h+\\frac{5}{12}d.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
