      ":question/problem": "![](images/d8/d806669f43dcf33cd2ddb1f31a6cbaa3436f06d116c7307375ad41ee30a6c371.png)\n\nIn the diagram, $F$ lies on the segment $RZ$. The given vectors are $\\overrightarrow{OR}=u$ and $\\overrightarrow{OZ}=e$. The lengths satisfy $RF:FZ=11:12$.\n\nExpress $\\overrightarrow{OF}$ in terms of $u$ and $e$. Fill in both coefficients, including their signs.\n\n$\\overrightarrow{OF}=$ {{field-1}} $u+$ {{field-2}} $e$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First express both endpoint vectors in the directions away from $O$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OR}=u\\qquad \\overrightarrow{OZ}=e .\n$$\n\nTrace the path from $R$ through $O$ to $Z$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{RZ}=\\overrightarrow{RO}+\\overrightarrow{OZ}=-u+e.\n$$\n\nThe ratio $RF:FZ=11:12$ gives $23$ parts in the whole segment. Thus\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{RF}=\\frac{11}{23}\\overrightarrow{RZ}=\\frac{11}{23}(-u+e).\n$$\n\nAdd along the path $O\\to R\\to F$ and collect coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overrightarrow{OF}&=\\overrightarrow{OR}+\\overrightarrow{RF}\\\\&=u+\\frac{11}{23}(-u+e)\\\\&=\\frac{12}{23}u+\\frac{11}{23}e.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
